# Day 23 - Style Tag and GitHub Pages

## 📚 Learning Objectives

* Learned how to use the style tag.
* Learned how CSS can be written inside HTML.
* Learned how to publish a website using GitHub Pages.

## HTML Tag Learned

### Style Tag

```html
<style>
</style>
```

Used to write CSS inside an HTML document.

## CSS Examples

```css
body{
    background-color: lightgray;
}

h1{
    color: blue;
}
```

## GitHub Pages

GitHub Pages allows a static website to be hosted directly from a GitHub repository.

## Practical Work

* Added a style tag.
* Styled a webpage.
* Enabled GitHub Pages.
* Published the website online.

## Key Takeaways

* CSS controls appearance.
* The style tag contains CSS rules.
* GitHub Pages can host static websites for free.
